<title>USA: Wyeth-Ayerst arthritis drug cleared by FDA.</title>
<headline>Wyeth-Ayerst arthritis drug cleared by FDA.</headline>
<dateline>RADNOR, Pa. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Home Products Corp said Tuesday that its Wyeth-Ayerst Laboratories division has been given FDA marketing clearance for a once-daily version of its arthritis medication.</p>
<p>The clearance was for Lodine XL, which is available in 400 mg and 600 mg tablets.</p>
<p>The company said this latest version may cost less than the original Lodine when cost is based on average wholesale price, which is a published list price and may not necessarily reflect actual price to pharmacists and consumers.</p>
</text>
